{
 "MonitoringProgramDescription": "Fifteen cameras at highway intersections and recreation sites around the Tahoe Basin count vehicles and people walking and biking, and log near misses and other safety events, using computer vision. Thirteen are permanent, and two were temporary.\n\nThe Tahoe Transportation District installed the cameras under a U.S. Department of Transportation SMART grant (Strengthening Mobility and Revolutionizing Transportation), with TRPA as the data partner. The record starts in March 2025.",
 "MonitoringApproach": "Derq's computer vision software reads each camera's video. It classifies what passes (passenger vehicles, trucks, buses, motorcycles, bicycles, and people walking) and counts them in 15-minute intervals by direction of approach. It also logs one record for each safety event, such as a near miss, wrong-way driving, or an illegal crossing.\n\nA TRPA script pulls the counts and events from Derq and loads them to the Transportation_SMART feature service on maps.trpa.org, replacing each day in full so that a rerun never duplicates records. Daily totals are the sum of the 15-minute vehicle counts.\n\nRead the totals with care. The cameras were switched on at different times, so a total is not comparable between cameras without allowing for the days each one counted. The speed table is one distribution for the whole Phase 1 record and is no longer updated. Three event names (lane change violation, turn violation, and stopped vehicle) are TRPA's reading of Derq's codes and are not yet confirmed with Derq.",
